# hw_frame.parm - real vehicle (MicoAir H743 V2 AIO), Week 5 S5-3.
#
# Load this file rather than typing parameters by hand. Hand entry is how a
# safety parameter goes missing, and half of these are safety parameters.
#
#   MAVProxy:  param load hw_frame.parm
#   readback:  ./scripts/hw_param_readback.py
#
# NO INLINE COMMENTS. MAVProxy breaks on them, and parm_file.parse_parm
# raises on them so the test suite catches it before the board does.
#
# Every value below is asserted by test_hw_config.py. Change one and the test
# tells you which invariant you broke.

# Frame. FRAME_CLASS 0 is the silent no-lift trap: a fresh EEPROM arms and
# accepts takeoff, then maxes throttle with zero lift.
FRAME_CLASS 1
FRAME_TYPE 1

# Geofence, SAFETY_CASE.md section 2. Type 3 = circle + altitude.
FENCE_ENABLE 1
FENCE_TYPE 3
FENCE_RADIUS 10
FENCE_ALT_MAX 5
FENCE_ACTION 1

# RTL_ALT is in CENTIMETRES; FENCE_ALT_MAX is in METRES. 400 cm = 4 m, which
# leaves 1 m of ceiling margin and still clears the 2 m takeoff altitude.
# ArduPilot's default of 1500 cm = 15 m is three times the fence ceiling, so a
# fence-breach RTL would climb straight through the fence it is responding to.
# check_fence_consistency asserts RTL_ALT/100 < FENCE_ALT_MAX.
RTL_ALT 400

# Failsafes. BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2 = RTL.
FS_THR_ENABLE 1
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2

# Kill-switch: motor emergency stop on its own dedicated momentary switch,
# never a shared or mode switch (SAFETY_CASE.md section 3).
RC7_OPTION 31
